+   "id": "e8f816bf-8669-44e5-8157-925d30c12231",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Lagrange's four-square theorem says every non-negative integer is a sum of four\n",
+    "squares. `Hu.four_squares(n)` finds the squares by building a quaternion of norm\n",
+    "$n$ from Hurwitz primes, so even huge $n$ takes only the cost of factoring it.\n",
+    "Jacobi's formula $r_4(n) = 8\\sum_{d \\mid n,\\ 4 \\nmid d} d$ counts the\n",
+    "representations (with order and signs), and `Hu.count_of_norm(n)` counts all\n",
+    "Hurwitz integers of norm $n$ (that includes the half-integer ones)."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "id": "428ae365-64c2-4aac-925c-5cec2090fdc7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "for n in [7, 310, 2026, 10**30 + 7]:\n",
+    "    a, b, c, d = Hu.four_squares(n)\n",
+    "    print(f\"{n} = {a}^2 + {b}^2 + {c}^2 + {d}^2   ({a*a + b*b + c*c + d*d == n})\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "def r4(n):                                  # Jacobi's four-square formula\n",
+    "    return 8 * sum(d for d in range(1, n + 1) if n % d == 0 and d % 4 != 0)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(\"\\nJacobi's count r4(n) matches the Lipschitz integers of norm n (n = 1..30):\",\n",
+    "      all(sum(h.is_lipschitz() for h in Hu.of_norm(n)) == r4(n) for n in range(1, 31)))\n",
+    "print(\"count_of_norm(n) matches the enumeration of all Hurwitz integers (n = 1..30):\",\n",
+    "      all(len(Hu.of_norm(n)) == Hu.count_of_norm(n) for n in range(1, 31)))"
+   ],
+   "execution_count": 52,
+   "outputs": [
